=20
PRODUCTS AND
PROJECTS
 [01] Paragent 3.0
(upgrade)=20
If your upstart is too small to have its own IT administrator, Paragent has
a product for you.  Paragent 3.0 is an open-source, SaaS-based IT
management application that provides real-time, on-demand data and
information about a company's networked computers.  The new release adds
automatic software and inventory collection, advanced search and remote
desktop functionality. Paragent claims to be one of the few SaaS companies
pursuing an open source strategy. http://www.paragent.com
 [02]
Linspire's Custom OS Build Service (new service)
Our friends at Linspire continue to find new niches, the latest being a
custom desktop Linux OS Build Service for its partners. The new
custom-build service is designed to help those partners not only to get the
exact feature sets they want but also cut their time to market and reduce
the expense involved in building a desktop Linux operating system.  One can
build a Debian or Ubuntu-based desktop Linux OS with customizable software
stacks and other features. http://www.linspire.com
 [03]
PostgreSQL 8.3 (update)
The PostgreSQL team is beamingly proud of the new Version 8.3 of the
popular high-performance, object-relational database management system.=20
Version 8.3 is said to provide greater consistency of performance than
previous editions, ensuring that every user can depend on the same high
performance demonstrated in recent benchmarks for every transaction. Other
enhancements include over 280 patches, Heap Organized Tuples, spread
checkpoints, background writer autotuning and asynchronous commit option -
all of which accelerate transaction processing throughput between 5-30%.=20
Many new features are included for application developers, as well.=20
PostgreSQL is available for download from the organization's Web site.http://=
www.postgresql.org
 [04] Permabit Enterprise Archive
Data Center Series=C2=A0 (new product line)
Heads up storage hounds, Permabit recently released Permabit Enterprise
Archive Data Center Series, a line of scalable data-reduced storage
solutions for enterprise archiving.  Permabit's proposition is that 60-80%
of data in the data center is static and sits on expensive,
transaction-optimized primary storage.  Their solution is to move large
volumes of static data to more cost-effective tiers with the same level of
assurance as primary storage.  The solutions scale up to 3 PB and offer
costs ranging from $0.33 to $2.33 per GB of storage, vs. $25 to 75 per GB
for competing archiving solutions, claims Permabit.  Permabit also says
that its new RAIN-EC data protection technology is 250 times safer than
RAID 6.  http://www.permabit.com

