THE BOOKSHELF

=20
[05] Up and Running With Joomla by
Skip Matheny & R. Allen Wyke (O'Reilly)
Up and Running With Joomla is O'Reilly's new Short Cut (brief PDF
document) on getting your Web team rolling in the same direction when
implementing the Joomla open-source CMS.  The resource shows how to
install, configure, customize, and extend a Joomla installation.  Up
and Running also offers a plethora of tricks and tips for managing
both customers and content authors.   http://www.oreilly.com
[06] C++ GUI Programming With Qt4, 2nd
Ed. by Jasmin Blanchette & Mark Summerfield
(Prentice-Hall)
Prentice-Hall says that C++ GUI Programming With Qt4 by Jasmin
Blanchette & Mark Summerfield, now in its second edition, is the book
that Trolltech uses to teach Qt to its own hires.  Essentially two
Trolltech insiders have written a start-to-finish guide to getting results
with Qt 4.3 so you can build industrial-strength C++ applications that run
natively on Windows, Linux/Unix, Mac OS X, and embedded Linux without
source code changes.  The book's approach is to use realistic examples and
in-depth advice, illustrating the best Qt programming patterns for nearly
every GUI development task, providing database access, integrating XML,
using subclassing, composition, and more.  http://www.informit.com

